{"_id":"68a7363d8ec3d8323af1f381","nodeId":"KJJ6PYjTnr_3yU2mNPL9v","roadmapSlug":"sql","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:40.099Z","description":"# UPDATE Statement\n\nThe UPDATE statement modifies existing data within a table. It allows you to change the values of one or more columns in a table, based on specified conditions. You can update a single row or multiple rows, and it's essential for keeping your database information accurate and current.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Efficient column updates in SQL","url":"https://www.atlassian.com/data/sql/how-to-update-a-column-based-on-a-filter-of-another-column","_id":"69bba6b933a0ad7a57afe6d4"}],"updatedAt":"2026-03-19T07:33:13.507Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d0416838","title":"DataCamp - SQL Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/ZVeXng"},{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d04167c7","title":"roadmap.sh - Master SQL","partner":"roadmap.sh","type":"course","url":"https://roadmap.sh/courses/sql"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/sql/content/KJJ6PYjTnr_3yU2mNPL9v.md"}